+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish sold uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; the
+  ingredients are consumed with the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>`. Tickets
+  already imported are skipped. The answer is `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }`
+  for what was imported (`dishes` counts dishes sold, the sum of `qty`). If a
+  row is invalid (`bad_request`) or an item runs out (`sale_not_enough_stock`)
+  nothing is imported and the message names the row (`row 2` is the first
+  data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item,
+  `theoretical` use from the sales sold in those days (inclusive), `actual`
+  use (every `consume` movement in those days) and `difference` (actual minus
+  theoretical), for items where either is above zero.
